# Screen designs — token rules (ADR 0075)

The design source is `screens/`: one frame per file, `screens/frames/<section>/<FrameId>.html`,
combined by `screens/index.html`. Shared styles, script and images live once in
`screens/screens.css`, `screens/screens.js` and `design-assets/`.

1. Find a frame: search `screens/index.html` for `id="<FrameId>"`, or use `design/CATALOG.md`.
2. Open **only** that frame's file. Never load every frame or `screens.css` unless the task is shared styling.
3. Edit a frame in its own file. Shared style or script goes in `screens.css` or `screens.js`, never
   copied into a frame. Images go in `design-assets/`, never inlined as base64.
4. Add a frame: copy a sibling file in the same section, rename it to the new id, and add its
   `gx-fig` block (caption, device chrome, iframe) to that section in `screens/index.html`.
5. Check: `npm run check:html -w @quran/design-tokens`. Render one frame:
   `python3 packages/design-tokens/scripts/frame-shot.py <FrameId> <out.png>`.
6. After any frame change, rebuild the reference (ADR 0087): `python3 design/screens/scripts/build.py && python3 design/scripts/build_reference.py`.
   A new design's `gx-cap` caption carries «(بانتظار الموافقة)» until the developer approves it. Review and share it at
   `design/<stack>/<Screen>/index.html` (light/dark × RTL/LTR × window sizes); no app code before approval.
   Share it as `design/<stack>/<Screen>/index.html?theme=light&dir=rtl&sizes=compact%2Cmedium%2Cexpanded%2Clandscape` (`theme` light|dark|both, `dir` rtl|ltr|both, `sizes` any of compact, medium, expanded, landscape).
7. Dark, LTR and tablet variants that nobody drew: `design/AGENTS.md` and `design/CATALOG.md`
   (generated from `screens/`; derived variants are drafts). Never edit `design/` by hand.
